WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.797
Classify information before moving it into a rented environment.

00:00:03.797 --> 00:00:08.315
Prompts and uploaded documents may contain credentials, personal records, source code,

00:00:08.315 --> 00:00:10.368
intellectual property, or regulated data.

00:00:10.368 --> 00:00:13.654
Model files may have license or distribution restrictions.

00:00:13.654 --> 00:00:18.172
Logs can reproduce prompt content, file paths, tokens, and request metadata.

00:00:18.172 --> 00:00:20.637
Confirm that the provider, account, region,

00:00:20.637 --> 00:00:24.333
and service type are approved for the data involved.

00:00:24.333 --> 00:00:28.852
Use identity and access management to grant the minimum permissions needed.

00:00:28.852 --> 00:00:31.316
Separate human administration from application identities.

00:00:31.316 --> 00:00:33.780
Protect SSH keys, rotate stale access,

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:37.888
and restrict firewall rules to known sources and required ports.

00:00:37.888 --> 00:00:39.120
A notebook, dashboard,

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:45.692
or inference server should not be exposed publicly without authentication simply because the rental is temporary.

00:00:45.692 --> 00:00:50.210
Store API keys, repository tokens, and credentials in a secrets mechanism,

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:54.728
not in shell history, notebooks, container images, or shared setup notes.

00:00:54.728 --> 00:00:59.246
Encrypt disks, object storage, snapshots, and network traffic according to policy.

00:00:59.246 --> 00:01:04.586
Minimize prompt logging, set retention periods, and control who can inspect operational data.

00:01:04.586 --> 00:01:10.747
Security responsibility remains with the renter even when the underlying hardware belongs to the provider.

00:01:10.747 --> 00:01:12.390
Plan deletion before upload.

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:16.086
At session end, remove temporary files, revoke short-lived credentials,

00:01:16.086 --> 00:01:21.426
and determine whether disks, snapshots, model caches, logs, object versions, or backups remain.

00:01:21.426 --> 00:01:24.712
Deleting an instance may not delete associated storage,

00:01:24.712 --> 00:01:29.230
while marketplace hosts may have different erasure assurances than major providers.

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:31.694
Record what was retained and why.

00:01:31.694 --> 00:01:34.980
A clean teardown protects both privacy and cost.
